---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/research.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research | Ethan Nguyen"
  description="Research projects and interests of Ethan Nguyen"
>
  <section class="page-heading">
    <h1>Research</h1>

    <p>
      My interests include scientific computing, computational physics,
      numerical methods, quantum computation, and high-performance computing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="research-section">
    <h2>Current Work</h2>

    <article class="research-item">
      <p class="research-type">Computational Physics · Julia</p>

      <h3>Monte Carlo Simulation of Ferroelectric ZrO₂</h3>

      <p>
        I am developing a lattice Monte Carlo simulation based on a six-state
        model for ferroelectric zirconia monolayers. The project includes energy
        calculations, periodic boundary conditions, Metropolis sampling, and
        state-distribution analysis.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="research-item">
      <p class="research-type">Computational Mathematics · Planned Research</p>

      <h3>Rubik’s Cube Algorithm Optimization</h3>

      <p>
        I am exploring how computational search, group theory, and numerical
        techniques can be used to analyze and optimize Rubik’s Cube algorithms.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="research-section">
    <h2>Research Interests</h2>

    <div class="interest-grid">
      <div>
        <h3>Scientific and High-Performance Computing</h3>
        <p>Numerical algorithms and software for complex scientific systems.</p>
        <p>Efficient scientific software for parallel computing systems.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3>Computational Physics</h3>
        <p>Simulations that connect physical models with computational methods.</p>
        <p>Hoping to work on quantum or astrophysics simulations with computational methods, showing things we can't experimentally show.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3>Quantum Computation</h3>
        <p>Quantum algorithms, simulation, and computational advantage.</p>
        <p>Simulate quantum aspects of the computer, whether that be the hardware or simulations on the computers.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3>Post-quantum cryptography</h3>
        <p>Mathematical number theory and cryptography to fight against quantum computers in the future.</p>
        <p>Protection based on the theoretical idea that quantum computers exist and can crack current RSA encryption.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>